From 87efef9278fe4a6946577c39ad8a1beda243afd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Surface the Pocket Casts Up Next queue as a podcast

The Up Next queue was only reachable as a read-only browse folder, so a
listener who started an episode on their phone had no way to continue it on a
Music Assistant speaker. It is now a podcast in the library, sitting with the
rest of the listening rather than among music playlists.

It is named "Pocket Casts: Up Next" because the library merges items whose
normalised names match and there is a real Pocket Casts show called "Up Next";
a subscriber to that show would otherwise find the queue folded into it. It
carries no artwork of its own, which falls back to the provider icon.

up_next/list now sends a body so the queue comes back ordered and carrying
playingStatus/playedUpTo, which gives each queued episode its resume point
without a second lookup. The queue is not a subscription, so its id is refused
for subscribe/unsubscribe rather than sent to Pocket Casts, which has no
podcast behind it. Its episodes keep naming the show they came from, since the
queue mixes shows.

The mixed-podcast episode conversion is now shared between the browse folders
and the queue; as a side effect In Progress, History and Starred pick up the
playback status their payloads already carried.
